  "historical_output_text": " I lugged on the worn out sneakers over familiar streets to where it always ended: an old brick path in our little cul de sacc that led to a forgotten park. This wasn't anything exciting or different from before - it just wasn’t a bad morning and there weren' any plans to get into trouble so a leisure morning stroll wasn’t such and unreasonable thing for someone in my shoes - but today I felt the world had a fresh perspective and everything had new meanings.\n\nAt one time my path led me straight towards an unremarkeworthy brick wall which had seen a lifetime’s use, now the same spot I always stopped at, now led a me an unrecognizable sight, an old man's bike. A rust red bicycle which was clearly old, yet well taken. It's frame seemed so delicate yet strong, its seat so low. The",
